From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:14:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-pcie: Keep the bootloader's PHY setup on the
 Inspiron 14 3420

On the Dell Inspiron 14 3420 (SC8180XP) the PCIe links to the NVMe drive
and the Wi-Fi card don't come up once the driver has reset the PHYs and
programmed its SC8180X init tables, while they work with the settings
the UEFI firmware leaves in place.

The driver already keeps the bootloader's setup when the PHY has a
no-CSR reset and the firmware left it started and powered up. Its
SC8180X PHYs have no no-CSR reset, so allow the same on this machine
when the firmware left the PHY started. A PHY the firmware didn't start
is still reset and programmed, and no other machine changes.

Suggested-by: Matt Durr <jmdurr@live.com>
Link: https://github.com/jmdurr/dell-inspiron-3420-arm
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
index da83358..60ec7a5 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
@@ -5683,13 +5683,16 @@ static int qmp_pcie_init(struct phy *phy)
 	/*
 	 * We can skip PHY initialization if all of the following conditions
 	 * are met:
-	 *  1. The PHY supports the nocsr_reset that preserves the PHY config.
+	 *  1. The PHY supports the nocsr_reset that preserves the PHY config,
+	 *     or it is on a machine whose PHYs only work with the
+	 *     bootloader's settings.
 	 *  2. The PHY was started (and not powered down again) by the
 	 *     bootloader, with all of the expected bits set correctly.
 	 * In this case, we can continue without having the init sequence
 	 * defined in the driver.
 	 */
-	qmp->skip_init = qmp->nocsr_reset &&
+	qmp->skip_init = (qmp->nocsr_reset ||
+			  of_machine_is_compatible("dell,inspiron-3420-sc8180xp")) &&
 		qphy_checkbits(pcs, cfg->regs[QPHY_START_CTRL], SERDES_START | PCS_START) &&
 		qphy_checkbits(pcs, cfg->regs[QPHY_PCS_POWER_DOWN_CONTROL], cfg->pwrdn_ctrl);
 
